<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal well-placed for euro - central banker.</title>
<headline>Portugal well-placed for euro - central banker.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal is well-placed to join the first wave of countries to take part in Europe's single currency, Bank of Portugal governor Antonio de Sousa told a Lisbon newspaper.</p>
<p>&quot;The (1997) budget -- with a lower deficit and substantial revenues from privatisations, which will allow for reductions in the public debt in a sustained way -- leads us to conclude that we are a strong candidate to join Economic and Monetary Union in 1999,&quot; De Sousa told Diario de Noticias in an interview.</p>
<p>Parliament is expected to pass the 1997 budget in a final vote on December 11.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
